# Line-ending policy (2026-10-12, the new-laptop migration; same as Map One's docs/174 fix of
# 2026-10-08): STORE EVERY FILE BYTE-FOR-BYTE, no conversion.
# Was `* text=auto eol=lf`. Files here are LF, CRLF or mixed (CLAUDE.md rule 9) and many build
# gates pin their exact bytes (sha-pinned manifests, receipts, generator --check outputs), so a
# clone that converted line endings would fail the first gate. `-text` also overrides Git for
# Windows' system core.autocrlf=true. Cost: a tool that flips a file's line endings shows as a
# whole-file change - commit it as written.
* -text

# Binaries - never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.flac binary
*.ogg binary
*.exr binary
*.tif binary
*.tiff binary
*.tga binary
*.dds binary
*.psd binary
*.iwi binary
*.xmodel_bin binary
*.xanim_bin binary
*.cast binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.7z binary
*.rar binary

# Blender masters and FBX sources ride Git LFS (as in Map One): GitHub refuses any file over
# 100 MB (the sky review masters are up to 223 MB) and every re-save of a master is a full copy.
# Free tier = 10 GiB storage + 10 GiB download / month, shared with Map One's LFS files.
*.blend filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.fbx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# The one music master over GitHub's 100 MB file limit (155.7 MB on 2026-10-12).
sound_assets/tod/music/tod_boss_music.wav filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
